15 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Infographic illustrating the connections between atopic dermatitis \(skin\) and allergic rhinitis \(nasal\), showing bidirectional and hypothesized pathways via type 2 immune activation and neuroimmune signaling. Candidate skin-to-nasal routes include neuroimmune signaling, epithelial alarmin signaling, shared inflammatory mediators, and scratching amplification. Candidate nasal-to-skin routes include sensory processes, upper airway irritation, sleep effects, shared mediators, and neural reflexes. System-level outcomes affected are sleep disturbance, fatigue, behavioral symptoms, quality of life reduction, and increased healthcare use. Diagram uses icons, arrows, and color coding to convey mechanism relationships and supporting evidence.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Infographic illustrating how external factors such as age, genetic susceptibility, allergens, infection, treatment, and scratching influence skin and nasal barrier dysfunction and local inflammation, with hypothesized cross-organ coupling. Mechanistic domains across both organs include microbiome regulation, epithelial barrier integrity and alarmin signaling, type 2 immune activation, and neuroimmune signaling, all interconnected by arrows representing biological relationships and contextual influences.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
